\title{Configuration}
\meta{toc}{false}

\p{Configuration records are frozen dataclasses. Build them through [pipeline helpers](api-pipelines.html), or use \code{dataclasses.replace} to change individual fields. Composable pipeline transforms construct validated \code{OptimizerConfig} instances for functional optimization.}

\<section>[id]{baux.OptimizerConfig}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.OptimizerConfig}[data-kind]{class}[data-module]{baux.turbo.config}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.OptimizerConfig}](api-configuration.html#baux.OptimizerConfig)}}
  \pre{
baux.OptimizerConfig(
    trust_region: TrustRegionConfig = TurboTrustRegion(),
    candidates: CandidateConfig = CandidateConfig(),
    init: InitConfig = InitConfig(),
    surrogate: Surrogate = NoSurrogate(),
    acquisition: AcquisitionConfig = RandomAcquisitionConfig(),
    acq_optimizer: AcqOptimizerConfig = RAASPOptimizerConfig(),
    observation_history: ObservationHistoryConfig = ObservationHistoryConfig(),
)
  }
  \p{The complete optimizer configuration.}
  \p{Frozen dataclass. Fields: \code{trust_region}, \code{candidates}, \code{init}, \code{surrogate}, \code{acquisition}, \code{acq_optimizer} and \code{observation_history}. Use \code{dataclasses.replace} to change fields.}
  \p{The default is a single TuRBO region, no surrogate and random acquisition. The [pipeline helpers](api-pipelines.html) construct compatible combinations.}
  \p{Surrogate choices include \code{ENNSurrogate}, \code{GaussianProcess}, \code{ExternalSurrogate} and \code{NoSurrogate}. Region choices include \code{TurboTrustRegion}, \code{MorboTrustRegion}, \code{RegionalSearchPolicy} and \code{NoTrustRegion}. Configuration records are in \code{baux.turbo.config}; commonly used types are also exported by \code{baux}.}
  \<div>[class]{api-example}{\<p>[class]{example-label}{Example}
\pre{
import numpy as np
import baux

bounds = np.array([[-1.0, 1.0], [-1.0, 1.0]])
pipe = baux.lhd(4) | baux.zero()
state = baux.init(bounds, pipe=pipe, seed=0)
assert isinstance(state.config, baux.OptimizerConfig)
assert state.num_observations == 0
}
  }
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/turbo/config/optimizer.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/turbo/config/optimizer.py#L51)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.RegionalSearchPolicy}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.RegionalSearchPolicy}[data-kind]{class}[data-module]{baux.region}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.RegionalSearchPolicy}](api-configuration.html#baux.RegionalSearchPolicy)}}
  \pre{
baux.RegionalSearchPolicy(
    count: int = 4,
    length: TrustRegionBounds = TrustRegionBounds(),
    success_tolerance: int = 3,
    failure_tolerance: int = 5,
    sharing: Literal["box_contain", "ellipsoid_ball", "nearest_center", "origin_only"] = "box_contain",
    allocation: Literal["incumbent_ucb1", "least_trials", "joint_acquisition"] = "incumbent_ucb1",
    restart_memory: Literal["fresh", "retain_relevant"] = "fresh",
    restart_center: RestartCenterPolicy = RestartCenterPolicy(),
    controller: Literal["turbo", "fixed_radius"] = "turbo",
    acquisitions: tuple[AcquisitionConfig | None, ...] = (),
)
  }
  \p{Configure region sharing, allocation and restart behavior.}
  \p{\code{count}, \code{success_tolerance} and \code{failure_tolerance} must be positive. \code{length} supplies normalized trust-region bounds.}
  \p{\code{sharing}: \code{"box_contain"}, \code{"ellipsoid_ball"}, \code{"nearest_center"} or \code{"origin_only"}. This constructor defaults to \code{"box_contain"}; the \code{regions()} helper defaults to \code{"ellipsoid_ball"}.}
  \p{\code{allocation}: \code{"incumbent_ucb1"}, \code{"least_trials"} or \code{"joint_acquisition"}. \code{controller}: \code{"turbo"} or \code{"fixed_radius"}.}
  \p{\code{restart_memory}: \code{"fresh"} or \code{"retain_relevant"}. \code{restart_center}: a \code{RestartCenterPolicy} from \code{baux.turbo.config.candidates}.}
  \p{\code{acquisitions}: empty to inherit the optimizer's rule, or a tuple with one acquisition configuration (or \code{None} to inherit) per region. Supported records are \code{UCBAcquisitionConfig}, \code{DrawAcquisitionConfig}, \code{ParetoAcquisitionConfig} and \code{RandomAcquisitionConfig} from \code{baux.turbo.config.acquisition}.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/turbo/config/trust_region.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/turbo/config/trust_region.py#L128)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.TrustRegionBounds}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.TrustRegionBounds}[data-kind]{class}[data-module]{baux.turbo.config}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.TrustRegionBounds}](api-configuration.html#baux.TrustRegionBounds)}}
  \pre{
baux.TrustRegionBounds(
    length_init: float = 0.8,
    length_min: float = 0.0078125,
    length_max: float = 1.6,
)
  }
  \p{Initial, minimum and maximum region lengths.}
  \p{Requires \code{0 < length_min <= length_init <= length_max}. Lengths are measured in normalized coordinates. Pass to a region policy or use \code{tr_bounds} in a pipeline.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/turbo/config/morbo_region.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/turbo/config/morbo_region.py#L16)}
}
